<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Combatdog built-in guns: part of the dog, like vanilla mechanoid guns (destroyed when dropped, never traded, never
       on a raider), picked per slot from the stable's Overview tab (user, 2026-10-20). Tier 4 instead has a fixed paired
       arsenal and a supplemental automatic smoke launcher (user, 2026-11-03). Stats copy the vanilla gun named here. -->
  <ThingDef Name="QR_BuiltInGunBase" ParentName="BaseGun" Abstract="True">
    <destroyOnDrop>true</destroyOnDrop>
    <tradeability>None</tradeability>
    <generateCommonality>0</generateCommonality>
    <relicChance>0</relicChance>
    <smeltable>false</smeltable>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
    <soundInteract>Interact_Rifle</soundInteract>
    <graphicData>
      <drawSize>(0.8,0.8)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <comps>
      <li>
        <compClass>Quadrunner.CompBuiltInGun</compClass>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>barrel</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>9</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
      </li>
    </tools>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="QR_BuiltInGunBase">
    <defName>QR_Gun_AssaultRifle</defName>
    <label>built-in assault rifle</label>
    <description>Hearthline's standard "settlement assurance" rifle mount. A familiar mechanism in a weatherproof housing, advertised as a reassuring presence along any property boundary. Reassurance is delivered in three-round bursts.\n\nA Combatdog's built-in assault rifle: balanced accuracy, good range and controlled bursts. Available in the primary gun slot of Tiers 2 and 3; select it in the stable's Overview.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Quadrunner/Weapons/AssaultRifle</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>500</MarketValue>
      <Mass>3.5</Mass>
      <AccuracyTouch>0.60</AccuracyTouch>
      <AccuracyShort>0.70</AccuracyShort>
      <AccuracyMedium>0.65</AccuracyMedium>
      <AccuracyLong>0.55</AccuracyLong>
      <RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.70</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
    </statBases>
    <verbs>
      <li>
        <verbClass>Verb_Shoot</verbClass>
        <hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
        <defaultProjectile>Bullet_AssaultRifle</defaultProjectile>
        <warmupTime>1.0</warmupTime>
        <range>30.9</range>
        <burstShotCount>3</burstShotCount>
        <ticksBetweenBurstShots>10</ticksBetweenBurstShots>
        <soundCast>Shot_AssaultRifle</soundCast>
        <soundCastTail>GunTail_Medium</soundCastTail>
        <muzzleFlashScale>9</muzzleFlashScale>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="QR_BuiltInGunBase">
    <defName>QR_Gun_LMG</defName>
    <label>built-in LMG</label>
    <description>A belt-fed Hearthline security mount for customers who considered the standard rifle's pauses an unnecessary courtesy. The brochure recommends it for "distributed access-denial requirements," beside a photograph of a very empty road.\n\nA Combatdog's built-in light machine gun. Its longer bursts trade accuracy and range for more shots, making it useful against groups. Available in the primary gun slot of Tiers 2 and 3; select it in the stable's Overview.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Quadrunner/Weapons/LMG</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>500</MarketValue>
      <Mass>8.5</Mass>
      <AccuracyTouch>0.40</AccuracyTouch>
      <AccuracyShort>0.48</AccuracyShort>
      <AccuracyMedium>0.35</AccuracyMedium>
      <AccuracyLong>0.26</AccuracyLong>
      <RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.6</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
    </statBases>
    <verbs>
      <li>
        <verbClass>Verb_Shoot</verbClass>
        <hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
        <defaultProjectile>Bullet_LMG</defaultProjectile>
        <warmupTime>1.8</warmupTime>
        <range>25.9</range>
        <ticksBetweenBurstShots>7</ticksBetweenBurstShots>
        <burstShotCount>6</burstShotCount>
        <soundCast>Shot_Minigun</soundCast>
        <soundCastTail>GunTail_Medium</soundCastTail>
        <muzzleFlashScale>9</muzzleFlashScale>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- Tier 4's fixed primary: two vanilla charge rifles on one mount, fired together by Quadrunner.Verb_PairedShoot. -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="QR_BuiltInGunBase">
    <defName>QR_Gun_DualChargeRifle</defName>
    <label>built-in paired charge rifles</label>
    <description>Two charge rifles on one reinforced Hearthline mount, wired to release their unstable pulses on the same trigger pull. The brochure describes the arrangement as "redundant enforcement"; the maintenance manual calls it two rifles.\n\nA Tier 4 Combatdog's fixed long-range weapon: the vanilla charge rifle's accuracy, burst, cycle and range, with two projectiles per shot. The dog switches to its paired chain shotguns within 20.9 cells.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Quadrunner/Weapons/DualChargeRifle</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <!-- Two stock charge rifles: vanilla accuracy, cycle, burst, range and projectile; mass and value are for the pair. -->
      <MarketValue>1000</MarketValue>
      <Mass>9.2</Mass>
      <AccuracyTouch>0.55</AccuracyTouch>
      <AccuracyShort>0.64</AccuracyShort>
      <AccuracyMedium>0.55</AccuracyMedium>
      <AccuracyLong>0.45</AccuracyLong>
      <RangedWeapon_Cooldown>2.00</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
    </statBases>
    <verbs>
      <li>
        <verbClass>Quadrunner.Verb_PairedShoot</verbClass>
        <hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
        <defaultProjectile>Bullet_ChargeRifle</defaultProjectile>
        <warmupTime>1.0</warmupTime>
        <range>27.9</range>
        <burstShotCount>3</burstShotCount>
        <ticksBetweenBurstShots>12</ticksBetweenBurstShots>
        <soundCast>Shot_ChargeRifle</soundCast>
        <soundCastTail>GunTail_Medium</soundCastTail>
        <muzzleFlashScale>9</muzzleFlashScale>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- Tier 4's fixed secondary: two vanilla chain shotguns, extended to 20.9 cells and more accurate (plan 0009). -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="QR_BuiltInGunBase">
    <defName>QR_Gun_DualChainShotgun</defName>
    <label>built-in paired chain shotguns</label>
    <description>Hearthline lengthened the barrels, tightened the choke and bolted two of them to the same cradle. The result keeps the chain shotgun's three-shell answer but reaches farther, and delivers it twice.\n\nA Tier 4 Combatdog's fixed close-range weapon: the vanilla chain shotgun's burst and cycle, extended to 20.9 cells with improved accuracy, and two projectiles per shot. The dog switches to it within 20.9 cells.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Quadrunner/Weapons/DualChainShotgun</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <!-- Two chain shotguns: the vanilla burst, cycle and projectile, with the plan's longer range and accuracy; mass
           and value are for the pair. -->
      <MarketValue>1000</MarketValue>
      <Mass>9.0</Mass>
      <AccuracyTouch>0.80</AccuracyTouch>
      <AccuracyShort>0.85</AccuracyShort>
      <AccuracyMedium>0.75</AccuracyMedium>
      <AccuracyLong>0.60</AccuracyLong>
      <RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.35</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
    </statBases>
    <verbs>
      <li>
        <verbClass>Quadrunner.Verb_PairedShoot</verbClass>
        <hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
        <defaultProjectile>Bullet_Shotgun</defaultProjectile>
        <warmupTime>1.2</warmupTime>
        <range>20.9</range>
        <burstShotCount>3</burstShotCount>
        <ticksBetweenBurstShots>10</ticksBetweenBurstShots>
        <soundCast>Shot_Shotgun</soundCast>
        <soundCastTail>GunTail_Heavy</soundCastTail>
        <muzzleFlashScale>9</muzzleFlashScale>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- Tier 4's supplemental mount: the vanilla smoke launcher, fired automatically by the parent implementation. It is
       equipmentType None so it cannot replace the damaging gun, and its verb is non-primary and non-interrupting. -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="QR_BuiltInGunBase">
    <defName>QR_Gun_SmokeLauncher</defName>
    <label>built-in smoke launcher</label>
    <description>A wide-bore smoke shell launcher fitted beside the paired guns, with its own loading mechanism and no interest in the dog's trigger discipline. Hearthline added it after customers complained that a deterrent was too easy to see coming.\n\nA Tier 4 Combatdog's automatic smoke launcher: launches vanilla smoke shells during combat without interrupting the charge rifles or chain shotguns. The launch interval is set on the tier, not by the weapon's cycle.</description>
    <equipmentType>None</equipmentType>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Quadrunner/Weapons/SmokeLauncher</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>500</MarketValue>
      <Mass>3.4</Mass>
      <RangedWeapon_Cooldown>4.5</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
    </statBases>
    <weaponClasses>
      <li>RangedHeavy</li>
    </weaponClasses>
    <verbs>
      <li>
        <verbClass>Verb_Shoot</verbClass>
        <hasStandardCommand>false</hasStandardCommand>
        <isPrimary>false</isPrimary>
        <nonInterruptingSelfCast>true</nonInterruptingSelfCast>
        <defaultProjectile>Bullet_SmokeLauncher</defaultProjectile>
        <warmupTime>0</warmupTime>
        <range>23.9</range>
        <forcedMissRadius>1.9</forcedMissRadius>
        <burstShotCount>1</burstShotCount>
        <soundCast>Shot_IncendiaryLauncher</soundCast>
        <soundCastTail>GunTail_Medium</soundCastTail>
        <muzzleFlashScale>14</muzzleFlashScale>
        <targetParams>
          <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
        </targetParams>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- Legacy only: Tier 4's former selectable minigun, superseded by the fixed paired arsenal (user, 2026-11-03). The def
       and its art stay so old saves and battle-history IDs resolve; no slot lists it and nothing can select it. -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="QR_BuiltInGunBase">
    <defName>QR_Gun_Minigun</defName>
    <label>built-in minigun</label>
    <description>Hearthline's premium answer to a question its sales department preferred not to record. The rotating barrel assembly required a reinforced mount, revised balance software and a much less friendly product photograph.\n\nA retired Tier 4 Combatdog mount: slow to spin up and inaccurate, but fires very long bursts at high speed, and its weight slightly reduces the dog's movement speed. New Tier 4 dogs carry the fixed paired arsenal instead; this weapon remains only for existing colonies and records.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Quadrunner/Weapons/Minigun</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>1200</MarketValue>
      <Mass>10</Mass>
      <AccuracyTouch>0.2</AccuracyTouch>
      <AccuracyShort>0.25</AccuracyShort>
      <AccuracyMedium>0.25</AccuracyMedium>
      <AccuracyLong>0.18</AccuracyLong>
      <RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.5</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
    </statBases>
    <weaponClasses>
      <li>RangedHeavy</li>
    </weaponClasses>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MoveSpeed>-0.25</MoveSpeed>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <verbs>
      <li>
        <verbClass>Verb_Shoot</verbClass>
        <hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
        <defaultProjectile>Bullet_Minigun</defaultProjectile>
        <warmupTime>2.5</warmupTime>
        <range>30.9</range>
        <burstShotCount>25</burstShotCount>
        <ticksBetweenBurstShots>5</ticksBetweenBurstShots>
        <soundCast>Shot_Minigun</soundCast>
        <soundCastTail>GunTail_Medium</soundCastTail>
        <muzzleFlashScale>9</muzzleFlashScale>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- Tier 3's second slot. Core has no flamethrower (design), and the Core assembly's spray verbs spawn DLC defs, so it
       is a short-range gun firing burning blobs: Flame damage sets what it hits alight. -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="QR_BuiltInGunBase">
    <defName>QR_Gun_Flamethrower</defName>
    <label>built-in flamethrower</label>
    <description>Originally catalogued by Hearthline as a vegetation-management attachment. Its reassignment to the security division changed the paint scheme, the warranty terms and very little else.\n\nA Tier 3 Combatdog's secondary weapon. Fires short-range bursts of burning fuel that can set targets alight; the dog switches to it automatically at close range. Fire can spread beyond the target, so keep it away from anything you want to preserve.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Quadrunner/Weapons/Flamethrower</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>600</MarketValue>
      <Mass>6</Mass>
      <AccuracyTouch>0.9</AccuracyTouch>
      <AccuracyShort>0.8</AccuracyShort>
      <AccuracyMedium>0.6</AccuracyMedium>
      <AccuracyLong>0.4</AccuracyLong>
      <RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.5</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
    </statBases>
    <verbs>
      <li>
        <verbClass>Verb_Shoot</verbClass>
        <hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
        <defaultProjectile>QR_Bullet_Flame</defaultProjectile>
        <warmupTime>0.8</warmupTime>
        <range>8.9</range>
        <burstShotCount>5</burstShotCount>
        <ticksBetweenBurstShots>6</ticksBetweenBurstShots>
        <soundCast>InfernoCannon_Fire</soundCast>
        <soundCastTail>GunTail_Light</soundCastTail>
        <muzzleFlashScale>12</muzzleFlashScale>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BaseBullet">
    <defName>QR_Bullet_Flame</defName>
    <label>burning fuel</label>
    <description>Burning fuel discharged by a Hearthline flamethrower. The service manual's advice is unusually direct: do not stand in front of the nozzle.\n\nAn incendiary projectile that deals flame damage and can ignite what it hits. It is not a stockpiled fuel item.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Projectile/LauncherShot</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <shaderType>TransparentPostLight</shaderType>
      <color>(254,140,40)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <projectile>
      <damageDef>Flame</damageDef>
      <damageAmountBase>9</damageAmountBase>
      <speed>30</speed>
      <ai_IsIncendiary>true</ai_IsIncendiary>
    </projectile>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- Medirunner foam sprayer (plan 0008): vanilla Gun_TurretFoam's spray on the dorsal mount. Foam is unlimited; each
       burst drains the dog's battery instead (RobodogWork.foamDrainPerBurst, Quadrunner.Verb_FoamSpray). -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="QR_BuiltInGunBase">
    <defName>QR_Gun_FoamSprayer</defName>
    <label>built-in foam sprayer</label>
    <description>Hearthline's insurers asked why the rescue model kept carrying people out of burning rooms and leaving the room burning. The answer was a compact firefoam pump drawing on the chassis battery, sold as standard equipment and priced as a premium feature.

A Medirunner's integrated foam turret. When a fire burns anywhere in the Home area, the network sends an available Medirunner to spray it out, after any rescues and during raids too. Foam is unlimited; every burst costs battery.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Quadrunner/Weapons/FoamSprayer</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>400</MarketValue>
      <Mass>5</Mass>
      <AccuracyTouch>1</AccuracyTouch>
      <AccuracyShort>1</AccuracyShort>
      <AccuracyMedium>1</AccuracyMedium>
      <AccuracyLong>1</AccuracyLong>
      <RangedWeapon_Cooldown>0.5</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <verbs>
      <li>
        <verbClass>Quadrunner.Verb_FoamSpray</verbClass>
        <defaultProjectile>Proj_Foam</defaultProjectile>
        <warmupTime>0.3</warmupTime>
        <range>14.9</range>
        <ticksBetweenBurstShots>2</ticksBetweenBurstShots>
        <burstShotCount>41</burstShotCount>
        <sprayWidth>5.5</sprayWidth>
        <sprayArching>1.5</sprayArching>
        <sprayThicknessCells>4</sprayThicknessCells>
        <sprayNumExtraCells>40</sprayNumExtraCells>
        <sprayEffecterDef>FoamSpray_Directional</sprayEffecterDef>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
